Z||000004||Will||06-04-2001||01:04 PM||||I meant to reply to this a while back, but forgot.<P>The Caprice uses the LT1 engine, which though extremely advanced, still uses a distribtor.<P>The biggest problem is that the LT1 electronics have only 1 coil output. Hence a distributor would need to be added to the engine.<BR>Another problem is that the LT1 distributor has essentially a 180x crank position signal, while the N* has a 24x signal.<P>My father and I talked about driving an LT1 distributor off the front of one of the cams, but I'm staying away from that until all the DIS solutions I'm considering fail.||||reg||1
